WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.987
Before anything else, LATYS needs at least one AI coding agent installed on your computer. Here's how to set up the big four on Windows: Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and Grok.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.943
First, you'll need a terminal. Search for PowerShell in the Start menu, or open one right here in LATYS.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:24.107
Claude Code first. Anthropic's setup page gives you a one-line PowerShell command. Paste it in, and press Enter.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.011
When it's done, run claude once, and sign in with your Anthropic account.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:46.414
Codex is just as quick. Copy the PowerShell command from OpenAI's Codex page, run it, then launch codex, and choose Sign in with ChatGPT.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:01:03.715
OpenCode installs with npm, so install Node.js first, if you don't have it. Then it's one command. Inside OpenCode, type slash connect to add a model.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:12.743
And for Grok, run xAI's installer from their Grok Build page, then grok login, to sign in.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:26.428
Back in LATYS, hit Re-check, and your agents are ready. If a command isn't found, just open a new terminal window first.
